From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:43:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: host: Add the iPad Air (J72) HSIC Wi-Fi transport

The A7's internal Wi-Fi, a BCM43241, sits on an HSIC port of one of the
SoC's EHCI controllers rather than on PCIe or SDIO. Nothing in the
kernel brings that port up: its HSIC PHY, the radio reset on the D2089
PMIC's GPIO3, the HOST_READY handshake GPIO and the root port the radio
enumerates on.

Add the J72 transport that does this: it powers the HSIC PHY, releases
the radio from reset, drives HOST_READY (GPIO 163), runs EHCI0 and
waits for the BCM43241 boot ROM on port 3, and can keep the controller
active for brcmfmac. It checks every register it writes against the
values measured on a J72 and refuses on a mismatch. It probes only on
request (confirm_native=1).

[Orchard: from thisiscamk/ipad-air-j72-linux 2a257d6,
 code/current/kernel/0001-j72-installed-kernel-snapshot.patch
 (drivers/usb/host/j72_wlan_transport_v3.c, j72-wlan-hcd.h and their
 Kconfig and Makefile entries), unchanged; commit message added.]
